# VNNI libz patch -- init rc fragment (Apache-2.0).
#
# GENERATED for build CL3B.260622.276.R4 / 16658739 by
#   vnni_patch.py ... --out-rc   (byte-identical copy of out/vnni.rc below the
#   next comment block).  Regenerate it for every build; never hand-edit.
#
# Binds the build-time-patched libz.so over /system/lib64/libz.so and
# /vendor/lib64/libz.so so adler32 takes its scalar path and never traps into the
# k15 VEX AVX-VNNI emulator.  Same /odm bind mechanism as the existing fstab /
# se_manifest binds in build_esp.py.
#
# OTA / other slot (review fix): each action is gated on the partition's build
# fingerprint, which init loads from the verified partition's own build.prop
# before early-init.  gb_slotsync builds the other slot's initrd from the SAME
# /gb/inject.gz after an A/B OTA, so this rc and /odm/vnni/* also run on the new
# build; there the fingerprint differs, the action never fires, and the stock
# libz runs under k15 emulation.  (Stock init.rc on this image uses the same
# `on early-init && property:` form.)
#
# Order: these actions must be parsed AFTER the gb.rc early-init action that
# mounts the /vendor overlay (bind /vendor -> /odm/vlower, overlay on /vendor);
# a bind made before it would be hidden by the overlay.  Appending this block to
# gb.rc (both trees) or installing it as /odm/etc/init/vnni.rc (parsed after
# gb.rc) satisfies that.  Do NOT put the vendor libz into /odm/vup instead: the
# overlay upper layer is not fingerprint-gated.
#
# The bind is remounted read-only after the relabel (restorecon needs it
# writable): the stock library lives on a read-only dm-verity partition.
#
# A process that mapped the stock libz before these actions (at most the
# short-lived apexd-bootstrap exec of stock init.rc's early-init, if it pulls libz
# in transitively; logd, the first direct libz user, starts in `on init`) keeps
# the stock copy and is simply emulated -- no correctness impact.

# vnni libz patch (generated by vnni_patch.py, Apache-2.0).
# Each bind fires ONLY on the exact build it was patched for:
# after an A/B OTA gb_slotsync reuses this initrd for the new
# slot, whose fingerprint differs, so nothing is bound there.
on early-init && property:ro.system.build.fingerprint=Android/desktop_system/desktop:17/CL3B.260622.276.R4/16658739:user/release-keys
    restorecon /odm/vnni/system_libz.so
    mount none /odm/vnni/system_libz.so /system/lib64/libz.so bind
    restorecon /system/lib64/libz.so
    mount none none /system/lib64/libz.so remount bind ro

on early-init && property:ro.vendor.build.fingerprint=ASUS/lapis/lapis:17/CL3B.260622.276.R4/16658739:user/release-keys
    restorecon /odm/vnni/vendor_libz.so
    mount none /odm/vnni/vendor_libz.so /vendor/lib64/libz.so bind
    restorecon /vendor/lib64/libz.so
    mount none none /vendor/lib64/libz.so remount bind ro
